                <pb facs="0677" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5449: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-06T13:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1928—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:08 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>113. Frequent reports have reached here about subscriptions which have been taken
                    up for Sandino in New York, Mexico City, Guatemala, Santiago, Chile, Buenos
                    Aires, and other places. General Feland requests that an effort be made to
                    ascertain where these funds are being sent and that every effort be made to
                    intercept any arms and ammunition which may be purchased with the funds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
